/Alt (Figure 4. For the 41 pooled units, what was coded on each question. The segments show the coded values, so a reader can see, for example, that one unit has a departmental concerted effort and 21 had none found, and that most course-review "yes" codes at faculty or university level are plans or recommendations rather than operating reviews. Read this as documentation found in a desk survey, not an adoption rate; the Q2 bar shows whether the word appears \(most units use it without defining it\), not whether it is defined, and "not assessable" means the search was not run.)
