6231 0 obj
<</Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/Alt (Figure 3. Among the 36 pooled units with at least one coded course, the number of units with a course per approach type, by whether the course belongs to the unit, its faculty, or the university. Courses linking Indigenous knowledge to Western science are the most widespread approach, especially at university level, while research-ethics content appears mostly in the units' own courses. A course can carry more than one approach; duplicate rows and sector-wide examples are excluded; "colonial harms in bioscience" counts only courses with bioscience content. Most cells are under five \(marked\), and the counts show which courses the survey could reach, not course quality or priority.)
/P 6230 0 R
/Pg 197 0 R
/K 8>>
endobj
